## Approval requirements (mirrors lifecycle transition roles)

| Change | Required approver(s) | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| Edit `schema/*.yaml` (vocabularies) | Knowledge Manager | Vocabulary changes affect every doc + the linter |
| Move a doc to `status: approved` | Peer reviewer + (ARB / Chief Architect) | Quality gates must pass |
| Move a doc to `status: baseline`/`frozen` | Knowledge Manager / Governance Board | Becomes canonical / change-controlled |
| Edit a `status: frozen` doc | Approved ADR required | Change control |
| Edit `Knowledge-Constitution.md` | ADR + ARB | Constitutional change |

## Review cadence

- Authoritative docs carry `next_review`; overdue reviews are flagged by `knowledge-lint`.
- Quarterly knowledge audit by the Knowledge Manager: orphans, duplicate authority, stale baselines, archive candidates.

## Rules

- Nothing becomes `authority: authoritative` without a recorded review (`reviewed_by`).
- AI-generated docs enter as `authority: generated` and require human review to be promoted.
- Exactly one authoritative document per (topic, bounded_context).
- Archive (never delete) obsolete, superseded, and duplicate material.
